[{"answer":"My sister had never been to Canada but came for a visit last April.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/1.mp3"},{"answer":"I picked her up at the airport in Toronto","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/2.mp3"},{"answer":"and drove her through the traffic and multilane highways,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/3.mp3"},{"answer":"past the grape vines and peach trees to Niagara Falls, where I live.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/4.mp3"},{"answer":"She was very tired from the flight and soon slept.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/5.mp3"},{"answer":"The first day we walked to see the Falls.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/6.mp3"},{"answer":"The spray from the Falls drifts high into the air and across the people standing to watch.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/7.mp3"},{"answer":"There are people from all over the world watching the water and using their cameras.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Because it was April there was still ice beside the water,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/9.mp3"},{"answer":"huge chunks of ice that looked like white rocks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/10.mp3"},{"answer":"In the river there were floating pieces of ice moving downstream.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/11.mp3"},{"answer":"The next day we went to the town where the Niagara River joins Lake Ontario.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/12.mp3"},{"answer":"The weather was warm.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/13.mp3"},{"answer":"We walked a long way and our feet were hot,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/14.mp3"},{"answer":"so we went down to the edge of the water to put our feet in.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/15.mp3"},{"answer":"One toe in was enough!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/16.mp3"},{"answer":"The water was so cold it made our feet ache!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/17.mp3"},{"answer":"A piece of ice drifted beside our feet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/18.mp3"},{"answer":"I put one foot in for a second then out,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/19.mp3"},{"answer":"as the pain of the cold went right through me!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/20.mp3"},{"answer":"My sister could not understand how it could be so warm, but there was still ice.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/21.mp3"},{"answer":"Another day we went to see my daughter;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/22.mp3"},{"answer":"she is living on a farm an hour's drive away.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/23.mp3"},{"answer":"We walked through her trees;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/24.mp3"},{"answer":"the buds were starting to turn into leaves.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/25.mp3"},{"answer":"We stopped and looked at the spring wildflowers.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/26.mp3"},{"answer":"We climbed across a creek by walking over a fallen tree.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/27.mp3"},{"answer":"We saw the footprints of raccoons by the water.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/28.mp3"},{"answer":"There was fresh air and sunshine and blue sky.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/29.mp3"},{"answer":"On the way home we stopped for hamburgers and fries at a drive-through restaurant.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/30.mp3"},{"answer":"She had never been to a drive-through restaurant before.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/31.mp3"},{"answer":"Then we went to a donut shop.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/32.mp3"},{"answer":"There are no donut shops where she lives.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/33.mp3"},{"answer":"There was a choice of 20 different types of donuts:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/34.mp3"},{"answer":"some round, some with holes, some with frosting,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/35.mp3"},{"answer":"some with jam inside, each was different.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/36.mp3"},{"answer":"The days passed quickly,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/37.mp3"},{"answer":"and soon it was time to take her back to the airport.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/38.mp3"},{"answer":"Some of the trees now had leaves;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/39.mp3"},{"answer":"some of the tulips were now blooming.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/40.mp3"},{"answer":"It was hard to say goodbye to my sister.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/41.mp3"},{"answer":"I hope we can visit again soon.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/143-my-sisters-visit-to-canada-2019-04-07-04-28-06/42.mp3"}]
